{"name":"Buff","hex":"#f0dc82","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Buff","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of the Buffs (Royal East Kent Regiment)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Buff"}],"entries":[{"title":"Buff (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Buff is the surname of:"},{"items":["Aaron Buff (1911–1994), American chair-maker","Charlotte Buff (1753–1828), youthful acquaintance of the German polymath Goethe, who fell in love with her","Conrad Buff II (1886–1975), Swiss-born American co-creator of illustrated children's books","Conrad Buff III (1926–1989), American architect, son of the above","Conrad Buff IV, American film editor, son of the above","Evelyn Buff-Segal (1913–2000), née Buff, American abstract expressionist painter","Joe Buff, American author of naval techno-thrillers","Johnny Buff (1889–1955), American boxer","Oliver Buff, Swiss footballer","Sebastian Buff (1828–1880), Swiss portrait painter","Wade Buff, a member of the 1950s The Dream Weavers vocal group","Xavier Buff, French mathematician"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buff_(surname)","wikidata":"Q37562632"},{"title":"Buff (nickname)","blocks":[{"text":"Buff is a nickname of:"},{"items":["E. U. Curtis Bohlen, former president of the World Wildlife Fund and former United States Assistant Secretary of State for Oceans and International Environmental and Scientific Affairs","Aldo Donelli (1907–1994), American football player and college and National Football League head coach, soccer player and college athletics administrator","Buff Hardie, a member of the Scotland the What? comedy review act","Geoff Hoon, British politician","Charles Kirkland, American retired basketball player","Buff Lord (1892–1985), English rugby league footballer","Bob McCready (1940–2007), Canadian box lacrosse goaltender","Buff Milner (1946–1996), New Zealand rugby union player","Buff Wagner (1897–1962), American football player"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buff_(nickname)","wikidata":"Q115800526"},{"title":"Buff (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Buff is a light brownish yellow, ochreous colour, typical of buff leather. Buff is a mixture of yellow ochre and white: two parts of white lead and one part of yellow ochre produces a good buff, or white lead may be tinted with French ochre alone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Chamois-natural.jpg/330px-Chamois-natural.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buff_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2085487"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Standard_Buff.jpg/250px-Standard_Buff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ea/Standard_Buff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Standard_Buff.jpg/250px-Standard_Buff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Buff after A. Maerz[9]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStandard_Buff.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Buff_after_R._Ridgway.jpg/330px-Buff_after_R._Ridgway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Buff_after_R._Ridgway.jpg/330px-Buff_after_R._Ridgway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Buff after R. Ridgway.[11]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABuff_after_R._Ridgway.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Sand_Drawings.JPG/250px-Sand_Drawings.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/co